{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"a95db423bda1c3216868b1c448e11daf49fd08eb213b639777270d5890ec4300","slug":"validation.index","location":"/validation/index.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Validation and quality assurance","label":"validation-hub","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Cornerstone Sustainability Data Initiative","given":"Cornerstone Sustainability Data","family":"Initiative"},"name":"Cornerstone Sustainability Data Initiative","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/cornerstone-data/eeio-docs","keywords":["EEIO","MRIO","input-output","emission factors","Scope 3","greenhouse gas"],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/cornerstone-data/eeio-docs/blob/main/validation/index.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/cornerstone-data/eeio-docs/edit/main/validation/index.md","thumbnail":"/eeio-docs/pr-preview/pr-28/build/quality-pipeline-3658fe840f4959968e4096f72dea67ca.svg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"index.md","url":"/eeio-docs/pr-preview/pr-28/build/index-645d11423edcb0586a1977f0bc7864d7.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","kind":"tip","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"U8APs2ItuP"}],"key":"eFWpeOUH4R"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation asks “did we build the model correctly?” It checks the code that builds the model, the data that go into it, and the model and emission factors that come out. Benchmarking, described in ","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"bffDqRGQi9"},{"type":"link","url":"/benchmarking","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why we benchmark","key":"RQ99CKoR5P"}],"urlSource":"../benchmarking/index.md","dataUrl":"/benchmarking.index.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"ziyD3dgwpY"},{"type":"text","value":", asks a different question: “are the results plausible compared with independent evidence?” Both feed into the next release.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"ylqPP1IdrA"}],"key":"I1KxZJVYJw"}],"key":"fr459f76kE"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/eeio-docs/pr-preview/pr-28/build/quality-pipeline-3658fe840f4959968e4096f72dea67ca.svg","alt":"Five boxes in a row show the build: acquire source data, transform (map, split, balance), build the model (A, L, B, D), calculate the emission factors, and publish the release files. Below them, a data validation band spans acquire and transform, a model validation band spans build, calculate and publish, and a code validation band spans all five steps. A note says benchmarking against independent evidence follows the build and feeds the next release.","key":"P2Gcuwzy7y","urlSource":"../figures/diagrams/quality-pipeline.svg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig-quality-pipeline","identifier":"fig-quality-pipeline","html_id":"fig-quality-pipeline","enumerator":"1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"snIU5ulBN1"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"DyypwLWr1H"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"Eg26a9gWmc"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"uTXvplYk98"},{"type":"text","value":"Where each kind of validation runs in the build. Code validation covers every step; data validation follows the data in; model validation checks what comes out.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"SleXto1FlN"}],"key":"kVRNzylOIT"}],"key":"P9AEap8VK4"}],"label":"fig-quality-pipeline","identifier":"fig-quality-pipeline","enumerator":"1","html_id":"fig-quality-pipeline","key":"SPxnMO5ZBs"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Code validation","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"iJYDQKIFwx"}],"identifier":"id-1-code-validation","label":"1. Code validation","html_id":"id-1-code-validation","implicit":true,"key":"JPRaB05O47"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model is built by open-source code, and every change to that code is tested before it is merged.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"ZCmXvilKju"}],"key":"Av1fyij6b1"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unit tests.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"oUXCfPQC9L"}],"key":"GhfsNpwXI3"},{"type":"text","value":" About 2,900 automated tests check individual steps against known answers. They include tests of the core formulas, such as ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"AFBrJxxXRV"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"N = D × L","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"l3fKeIrCXt"},{"type":"text","value":", and of the conservation rules the methods rely on: when emissions or output are split, mapped or reallocated, the totals before and after must match. Small worked examples, including a toy model of ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"U1fIUXwGXv"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"ABSR","identifier":"term-absr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ABSR","key":"vr1TOmC5yk"}],"kind":"definitionTerm","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"term-absr","remote":true,"url":"/reference/glossary","dataUrl":"/reference.glossary.json","key":"jLpkTdbAZb"},{"type":"text","value":" and of ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"mqxVR5yDVk"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"RAS","identifier":"term-ras","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RAS","key":"rqzTZHg7iT"}],"kind":"definitionTerm","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"term-ras","remote":true,"url":"/reference/glossary","dataUrl":"/reference.glossary.json","key":"t8FvsThT52"},{"type":"text","value":" balancing, are solved by hand and checked against the code.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"aZwUQWZCNB"}],"key":"uJJp5v5D1G"}],"key":"QZdpoWnz4C"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema checks.","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"FMo6npituF"}],"key":"fq29sweV2V"},{"type":"text","value":" The main tables are checked for their structure every time they are built: the full list of 405 sectors in the right order, every country present, no duplicates, and no missing values. Final demand and exports must not be negative.","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"P0S74waGqt"}],"key":"OUN5b6dywK"}],"key":"uCog5OVXNj"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Integration and regression tests.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"hXonT704KD"}],"key":"gesnaKea8t"},{"type":"text","value":" Larger tests rebuild whole parts of the model, such as the U.S. tables, the GHG extension, and the global ","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"m08TeVYcwP"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"B","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"iSllEYbb6S"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"SDhjobQuKv"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"M","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"iik04dYmcg"},{"type":"text","value":" matrices, and compare them with a pinned reference result from the release build. A change that moves any value by more than 0.01% fails the test, so every change to the results is deliberate and reviewed. The longest of these tests run on a schedule every weekday.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"lf0etz6WKV"}],"key":"IyPT8utwSU"}],"key":"A976mCm2JS"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code quality.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"Lq2i739fxO"}],"key":"DonHy2X8RM"},{"type":"text","value":" Each proposed change is checked automatically for formatting, coding errors and type consistency before the tests run.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"pKyDRaon1L"}],"key":"IRtOtDOqPg"}],"key":"jKselazixT"}],"key":"kzyEiXZWhb"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Data validation","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"DU11Ejmxg8"}],"identifier":"id-2-data-validation","label":"2. Data validation","html_id":"id-2-data-validation","implicit":true,"key":"uU7EuvxECN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data are checked when they arrive, as they move through each step of the build, and against references.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"XcoggQXSye"}],"key":"YpLPlknAFi"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"On arrival","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"g3rG5PNDv2"}],"identifier":"on-arrival","label":"On arrival","html_id":"on-arrival","implicit":true,"key":"zXE3FC2maR"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structure and coverage.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"NFi2nnkumv"}],"key":"i6kR8z5nZq"},{"type":"text","value":" Each source is checked for the countries, sectors, years and units it should contain. A source that is missing a country or sector the model needs is rejected rather than filled silently.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"iNL6zHivJE"}],"key":"uMFCZfgniS"}],"key":"rfjg84qzB8"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internal consistency.","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"l9Rjcy4snZ"}],"key":"MvCZqXJhCL"},{"type":"text","value":" Published identities in the source are checked before the data are used. For example, the accounting identities of the FIGARO tables must be satisfied, each sector’s emissions in the OECD data must add up to the published total, and the BEA tables are checked against BEA’s own benchmark panel and sign conventions.","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"PZDQBjMxQv"}],"key":"hwTvtSVoak"}],"key":"c8Crz2ZHnf"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reproducibility.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"rWpNSvAsSs"}],"key":"a4zQttxSaw"},{"type":"text","value":" Extracted datasets are regenerated from the original source and compared with the stored copy, and stored copies older than the method that made them are flagged.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"mQdgFS4fkl"}],"key":"Zg0zqnPATS"}],"key":"svYH4GxXwx"}],"key":"Tz7QNNblu0"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Through each transformation","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"kXeJFKoD23"}],"identifier":"through-each-transformation","label":"Through each transformation","html_id":"through-each-transformation","implicit":true,"key":"H0SudUQ8pU"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Totals are kept.","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"PBJM4IdYjf"}],"key":"O6NFOIAcYe"},{"type":"text","value":" When a source sector is split, allocated to the 405 common sectors, or reallocated between sectors, each country’s total for each source sector is kept. An independent calculation maps the final results back to every source cell and fails if they do not match (see ","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"mel8RyF2Rr"},{"type":"link","url":"/ee","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The GHG extension: overview","key":"R7X5y9l6Fv"}],"urlSource":"../ee/index.md","dataUrl":"/ee.index.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"sqqJmxB1E3"},{"type":"text","value":").","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"fC1xqtanpd"}],"key":"BKMhsEbJ8r"}],"key":"k8V30fgd3h"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tables balance.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"wh4kU85BK1"}],"key":"alBrEWtuj8"},{"type":"text","value":" The U.S. Supply and Use tables are balanced so that for every commodity, supply equals use, along with industry output, taxes, subsidies, margins and value added. The multi-region table is balanced with ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"BDZx6rLD67"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"RAS","identifier":"term-ras","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RAS","key":"BGeibx530d"}],"kind":"definitionTerm","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"term-ras","remote":true,"url":"/reference/glossary","dataUrl":"/reference.glossary.json","key":"s1DojPDSpC"},{"type":"text","value":" so that each country’s sales match its output within 0.1%; a run that cannot meet a looser 1% limit fails instead of being published. Final demand implied by the balanced table must not be negative.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"l9KSvuuuA5"}],"key":"o17H9tlEVQ"}],"key":"RmpYZ6G23A"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Facility data set a floor.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"xlN2rltcr2"}],"key":"QzhEw7nnKr"},{"type":"text","value":" For U.S. sectors, CO₂, CH₄ and N₂O are not allowed to fall below what the sector’s own facilities report to EPA’s Greenhouse Gas Reporting Program (","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"GMitNUkDod"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"GHGRP","identifier":"term-ghgrp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GHGRP","key":"DSqOZ20aMX"}],"kind":"definitionTerm","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"term-ghgrp","remote":true,"url":"/reference/glossary","dataUrl":"/reference.glossary.json","key":"tnBvDEu7zy"},{"type":"text","value":"). Sectors whose facilities are almost all covered by the program are also capped from above. Each national inventory total is unchanged by these adjustments.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"z5mqxxRABJ"}],"key":"sVL30Tiety"}],"key":"kt8kzuLdF6"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"No missing or invalid values.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"JMPXUrM5j8"}],"key":"OOtUHWRsrd"},{"type":"text","value":" Values are checked for missing, infinite or negative numbers where they are not allowed, and a calculation that would leave a gas or a country empty stops with an error. How the few negative values in source data are treated is recorded case by case.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"Mmb1mpiET9"}],"key":"WiRyAkzC2o"}],"key":"h1lpMMW45Q"}],"key":"qpNT3txVyA"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Against references and other years","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"oa0qYqhcp4"}],"identifier":"against-references-and-other-years","label":"Against references and other years","html_id":"against-references-and-other-years","implicit":true,"key":"r20yKaUaHT"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other years of the same data.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"k29WDXmdTf"}],"key":"yUEmJ2GnrB"},{"type":"text","value":" Each data update is compared with the previous year of the same source, checking sector counts, totals, and which sectors move most. Over the U.S. time series from 2017 to 2024, changes in emissions are checked against changes in output, sector by sector.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"xEMQ02NMDo"}],"key":"eUX83HGDjD"}],"key":"GKCDUcwGDn"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other sources.","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"CCBEhSJws2"}],"key":"Q0HkkLiuDo"},{"type":"text","value":" The model’s U.S. emissions by sector are compared with facility totals from GHGRP. Where two sources cover the same countries, as FIGARO and the OECD tables do for 45 countries, they are compared sector by sector before one is chosen (see ","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"WwrzfrxBIG"},{"type":"link","url":"/reference/methods-by-country","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods by country","key":"jWUeBDzLmE"}],"urlSource":"../reference/methods-by-country.md","dataUrl":"/reference.methods-by-country.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"qjkwXruv4U"},{"type":"text","value":").","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"Hs5LH1IriP"}],"key":"APDi4xMzOU"}],"key":"AkOBhLT43w"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gaps.","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"mnP9UHyQNZ"}],"key":"mj7G7JrBEj"},{"type":"text","value":" Coverage is checked for every country and sector. Where a country has no output or no emissions for a sector, its emission factor is filled from its region, as described in ","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"MhgVDlvrjf"},{"type":"crossReference","url":"/factors/calculation","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filling missing country factors","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"tw3jW7LC1d"}],"urlSource":"../factors/calculation.md#filling-missing-country-factors","dataUrl":"/factors.calculation.json","identifier":"filling-missing-country-factors","label":"filling-missing-country-factors","remote":true,"protocol":"file","kind":"heading","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"filling-missing-country-factors","key":"rfSL9gtDCA"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"tUbikQyDdE"}],"key":"QN1weKCKwz"}],"key":"NdmmCwivzB"}],"key":"EwSuJaz0oI"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Model validation","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"vU8zFOkt76"}],"identifier":"id-3-model-validation","label":"3. Model validation","html_id":"id-3-model-validation","implicit":true,"key":"Vw8CC7UvK7"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model as a whole is checked by asking whether it reproduces the data it was built from, and how its results compare with previous models.","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"S8L8qHYLMa"}],"key":"fnwz3kTztY"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":5